<header class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/programmes/">Programmes and events</a></p>
    <h1>Savings for Future: building resilience among small-scale fish processors</h1>
    <p class="lede">Women who dry and process fish carry much of the risk in coastal economies. This project helps them save, plan for climate shocks and earn more from what they make.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <dl class="facts" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
      <div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Kudawella (Tangalle), Negombo and Ambalangoda</dd></div>
      <div><dt>When</dt><dd>2024</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Who</dt><dd>Women small-scale fish processors</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Led by</dt><dd>Department of Agribusiness Management, Faculty of Agricultural Sciences, Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Funded by</dt><dd>Australia Awards Sri Lanka, small grant scheme</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Forum’s role</dt><dd>Community engagement and links with local fishing communities</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Savings for Future aims to strengthen the resilience and financial wellbeing of women fish processors by promoting climate resilience, financial inclusion and sustainable livelihoods.</p>
      <p>A series of capacity-building workshops introduces participants to a mobile savings application, built for the project, and builds their knowledge of:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>climate change impacts and adaptation</li>
        <li>financial literacy and access to formal financial institutions</li>
        <li>alternative livelihoods and value addition</li>
        <li>safety and quality in fish processing</li>
        <li>market creation and entrepreneurship</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The forum supports the project by facilitating engagement with the communities and strengthening collaboration with local fisheries organisations. Together, the partners aim to give women fish processors the knowledge, skills and financial tools to build resilient livelihoods.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

